 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Searching mathlib/Mathlib/MeasureTheory for `dirac_le|le_dirac` finds only `le_dirac_apply` and `measurable_dirac`, so no such iff exists. Mathlib's `Measure.sub_add_cancel_of_le` (Measure/Sub.lean:100) requires `\u03bd \u2264 \u03bc`. Adding then removing is already covered by `Measure.add_sub_cancel` (Measure/Sub.lean:105).",
   "file": "TauCeti/MeasureTheory/Measure/Sub.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public `dirac_le_iff_one_le_apply_singleton : dirac x \u2264 \u03bc \u2194 1 \u2264 \u03bc {x}` (under `MeasurableSingletonClass`), use it in `sub_dirac_apply_singleton`, and add `sub_dirac_add_dirac_of_one_le (h : 1 \u2264 \u03bc {x}) : \u03bc - dirac x + dirac x = \u03bc`.",
   "issue": "`sub_dirac_apply_singleton` proves `dirac x \u2264 \u03bc` from `1 \u2264 \u03bc {x}` only as an inline `have hle`. Without it in the public API, the reinsertion identity `\u03bc - dirac x + dirac x = \u03bc`, which recursive occurrence removal needs, cannot be reached through Mathlib's `Measure.sub_add_cancel_of_le`.",
   "line": 52
  }
 ],
